@startuml Builder Pattern - Commission Calculator

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Builder Pattern - Deal Builder Implementation

' Product - Domain Model
class Deal <<Product>> {
  -id: String
  -title: String
  -value: BigDecimal
  -status: DealStatus
  -salesRepId: String
  -products: List<DealProduct>
  -closeDate: LocalDate
  -createdDate: LocalDate
  -lastModifiedDate: LocalDate
  +Deal(title: String, value: BigDecimal, salesRepId: String)
  +getId(): String
  +getTitle(): String
  +getValue(): BigDecimal
  +getStatus(): DealStatus
  +setStatus(status: DealStatus): void
  +getProducts(): List<DealProduct>
  +setProducts(products: List<DealProduct>): void
}

' Builder
class DealBuilder <<ConcreteBuilder>> {
  -id: String
  -title: String
  -value: BigDecimal
  -status: DealStatus
  -salesRepId: String
  -products: List<DealProduct>
  -closeDate: LocalDate
  -createdDate: LocalDate
  -lastModifiedDate: LocalDate
  +DealBuilder(title: String, value: BigDecimal, salesRepId: String)
  +withId(id: String): DealBuilder
  +withStatus(status: DealStatus): DealBuilder
  +addProduct(product: DealProduct): DealBuilder
  +withProducts(products: List<DealProduct>): DealBuilder
  +withCloseDate(closeDate: LocalDate): DealBuilder
  +withCreatedDate(createdDate: LocalDate): DealBuilder
  +withLastModifiedDate(lastModifiedDate: LocalDate): DealBuilder
  +build(): Deal
}

' Director
class DealDirector <<Director>> {
  -builder: DealBuilder
  +DealDirector(builder: DealBuilder)
  +changeBuilder(builder: DealBuilder): void
  +constructStandardDeal(): Deal
  +constructPremiumDeal(): Deal
  +constructWonDeal(): Deal
  +constructLostDeal(): Deal
}

' Supporting Classes
class DealProduct <<ValueObject>> {
  -productId: String
  -name: String
  -quantity: int
  -price: BigDecimal
}

enum DealStatus <<Enum>> {
  OPEN
  WON
  LOST
  PENDING
}

' Relationships
DealBuilder ..> Deal : creates
DealDirector o--> "1" DealBuilder : uses
DealDirector ..> Deal : returns
Deal o--> "*" DealProduct : contains
Deal --> "1" DealStatus : has status

' Pattern component notes
note right of Deal
  <b>Product: Deal</b>
  Complex domain object representing
  a sales deal/opportunity.

  <b>Complexity Factors:</b>
  • 9 attributes (3 required, 6 optional)
  • Collection of DealProduct objects
  • Multiple date fields with defaults
  • Status lifecycle management

  <b>Why Builder is Useful:</b>
  • Avoids telescoping constructors
  • Makes object creation readable
  • Handles optional parameters cleanly
  • Ensures consistent object state

  <b>Example Without Builder:</b>
  new Deal("title", value, "rep", id,
    status, products, closeDate,
    createdDate, modifiedDate)
  → Hard to read, easy to mix up params
end note

note left of DealBuilder
  <b>Concrete Builder: DealBuilder</b>
  Fluent interface for constructing Deal objects.

  <b>Constructor Requirements:</b>
  Only requires essential fields:
  • title (String)
  • value (BigDecimal)
  • salesRepId (String)

  <b>Fluent Methods:</b>
  Each withXxx() method:
  • Sets a property value
  • Returns 'this' (DealBuilder)
  • Enables method chaining

  <b>Build Process:</b>
  1. Constructor stores required fields
  2. Fluent methods set optional fields
  3. build() creates and configures Deal
  4. Returns fully-constructed Deal

  <b>Design Decisions:</b>
  • addProduct() - adds single product
  • withProducts() - replaces all products
    (creates defensive copy)
  • Default values set in builder fields:
    status = OPEN
    createdDate = LocalDate.now()
    lastModifiedDate = LocalDate.now()
end note

note bottom of DealDirector
  <b>Director: DealDirector</b>
  Encapsulates common Deal construction
  sequences for reusability.

  <b>Predefined Constructions:</b>
  • <b>constructStandardDeal()</b>
    → OPEN status, 30-day close date

  • <b>constructPremiumDeal()</b>
    → OPEN status with premium products
    → 15-day close date (faster sale)

  • <b>constructWonDeal()</b>
    → WON status, close date in past

  • <b>constructLostDeal()</b>
    → LOST status, close date in past

  <b>Benefits:</b>
  • Reuses common construction logic
  • Hides complexity from clients
  • Ensures consistent configurations
  • Reduces code duplication

  <b>Flexibility:</b>
  changeBuilder() allows switching to
  different DealBuilder instances while
  reusing same construction methods.
end note

note bottom of DealProduct
  <b>Value Object</b>
  Represents a product/item
  within a deal.

  Used by DealBuilder to
  populate Deal.products
  collection.
end note

note right of DealStatus
  <b>Enum</b>
  Lifecycle states for
  a sales deal.

  Builder can set any
  valid status value.
end note

' Usage examples note
note top of DealBuilder
  <b>Usage Example - Fluent API:</b>

  Deal deal = new DealBuilder("Software Deal",
                new BigDecimal("10000"), "SALES-001")
      .withId("DEAL-123")
      .withStatus(DealStatus.OPEN)
      .addProduct(product1)
      .addProduct(product2)
      .withCloseDate(LocalDate.now().plusDays(30))
      .build();

  <b>Advantages:</b>
  ✓ Readable, self-documenting code
  ✓ Clear what each parameter is
  ✓ Only specify needed attributes
  ✓ Can't mix up parameter order
  ✓ Type-safe at compile time
end note

note bottom of DealDirector
  <b>Usage Example - Director:</b>

  DealBuilder builder = new DealBuilder(
      "Enterprise Deal",
      new BigDecimal("50000"),
      "SALES-002");

  DealDirector director = new DealDirector(builder);

  // Use predefined construction sequence
  Deal standardDeal = director.constructStandardDeal();
  Deal premiumDeal = director.constructPremiumDeal();

  <b>When to Use Director:</b>
  • Need consistent configurations
  • Multiple clients build same way
  • Complex construction sequence
  • Want to hide construction details
end note

' Legend
note right of DealBuilder
  <b>Builder Pattern in Commission Calculator:</b>

  <b>Problem Solved:</b>
  Deal objects have many optional parameters.
  Traditional constructors would require:
  • Multiple overloaded constructors
    (telescoping constructor anti-pattern)
  • Or setters on mutable object
    (breaks immutability, allows invalid state)

  <b>Builder Solution:</b>
  • Separates Deal construction from representation
  • Provides fluent, readable API
  • Handles required vs. optional parameters
  • Creates fully-initialized objects
  • Enables method chaining

  <b>Implementation Pattern:</b>
  1. <b>DealBuilder</b> is static nested class
     in BuilderPatternImplementation
  2. Constructor takes required parameters
  3. Fluent methods set optional parameters
  4. build() creates final Deal object

  <b>Key Benefits in This Domain:</b>
  • Test data creation is very clean
  • Different deal types (standard, premium)
    are easy to construct
  • Director provides reusable templates
  • Easy to add new optional fields
  • Improves code readability

  <b>Pattern Variations Used:</b>
  • Constructor with required params
  • Default values for optional params
  • Defensive copying (withProducts)
  • Director for common configurations
end note

@enduml
